  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CORRIDORS &amp; COMMUNITIES: CONS VITAL FOREST HABITAT IN N HONDURAS IV</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will strengthen the capacity of local institutions to manage 75,000 hectares of forest in and around Pico Bonito National Park (PBNP) and in the corridor connecting PBNP with the Texiguat Wildlife Refuge and Cuero y Salado National Park in northern Honduras. It will also: 1) reforest 1,500 hectares with native trees; 2) establish new environmental funds for forest protection; 3) reduce anthropogenic pressure on bird habitat; 4) establish 22 ha of agroforestry plots; 5) implement silvopastoral systems on 20 ha; and 5) increase appreciation for forest habitat among the local community.</narrative>
  </description>
